{"Using forEach(async ...) does not await the async body, so deletions may run in the background and errors can become unhandled/reordering-prone. Should use await Promise.all(filtered.map(async ...)) or a for...of loop with await to ensure completion and consistent error handling.": 0.9497402310371399, "The appStore uses import() directly in the object literal, which eagerly starts loading every app module at initialization time. If lazy loading is intended, should store functions like () => import('./applecalendar') and invoke them only when needed to avoid increased startup time and memory usage.": 0.7967411875724792, "getCalendar is now async and getCalendarCredentials stores the returned Promise as calendar. Need to ensure downstream usage consistently treats item.calendar as a Promise and that types reflect that, and that no other call sites still assume calendar is a synchronous Calendar | null.": 0.9137587547302246}